Context
  Decided to keep the core name after surveying claude-plugins-official: the -skills
  suffix is a live vendor convention there (18 of 314 entries keep it), so the suffix
  was never the problem -- the doubling in /guile-skills:guile-repl-server was. The
  user's reason for keeping the core name is the stronger one I had missed: gh skill,
  the plugin and the marketplace are three distribution channels that all key off it.

Deviations
  Script filenames and the workspace artifacts were left alone, both deliberately and
  for different reasons -- blast radius in the first case, not falsifying a record in
  the second.

  The cost accepted: a standalone `gh skill install dsp-dr/guile-skills repl-server'
  lands a skill whose NAME no longer says Guile. Mitigated only by the repo being
  named in the command and by every skill's description and compatibility fields
  stating it. Recorded in issue #16 rather than left implicit.

Considerations
  The validators are what made this safe to do mechanically. Three cross-checks over
  four identities meant the sweep could not be half-finished silently, and that is the
  first time the calibration work paid for itself on a change of this size.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, guile3 3.0.10, Claude Code 2.1.261, as
  dsp-dr. 23 files swept, 4 renamed, 64 workspace files untouched. gmake checks green;
  ship-check green; 3 labels created.
